{"parentUuid":"9ed16a6a-3dab-483f-b6e0-0eff5ca4193f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a17047a6cc88ea783","message":{"id":"9713c46b-837b-4973-930e-d959a165da00","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to provide a status update before continuing with the task. Let me respond to the coordinator's message first, then continue with the implementation plan.\n\nI'll let the coordinator know I'm working on analyzing the PRD and creating the implementation plan, and I'll share what I've found so far. Then I'll continue with the detailed breakdown.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":100,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"22091c0c-187e-42a9-9c89-382602606527","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:51:14.649Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack","sessionId":"bf17b420-9618-43bc-84f2-60c55630bfc5","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"22091c0c-187e-42a9-9c89-382602606527","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a17047a6cc88ea783","message":{"id":"9713c46b-837b-4973-930e-d959a165da00","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1499b1ac-32ef-490e-9ad0-8931474117f4","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"main","message":"I'm analyzing the PRD document at C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack\\bank-dashboard\\03-A-risk-engine-and-bank.md to understand what needs to be built. I've created the directory structure for scoring/, bank/, and data/ folders. Now I'm breaking down the work into components that can be worked on in parallel by multiple agents, focusing on the classical risk engine (scoring/), synthetic bank (bank/), data handling, and following the build order requirements (A-01 through A-15, BK-01 through BK-10). I'll provide a detailed implementation plan shortly.","summary":"Analyzing PRD and creating implementation plan","type":"message","recipient":"main","content":"I'm analyzing the PRD document at C:\\Users\\R.NETH…"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":100,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"wireToolInputs":{"call-1499b1ac-32ef-490e-9ad0-8931474117f4":{"to":"main","message":"I'm analyzing the PRD document at C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack\\bank-dashboard\\03-A-risk-engine-and-bank.md to understand what needs to be built. I've created the directory structure for scoring/, bank/, and data/ folders. Now I'm breaking down the work into components that can be worked on in parallel by multiple agents, focusing on the classical risk engine (scoring/), synthetic bank (bank/), data handling, and following the build order requirements (A-01 through A-15, BK-01 through BK-10). I'll provide a detailed implementation plan shortly.","summary":"Analyzing PRD and creating implementation plan"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"abcef535-216d-437e-ba51-8415e549915b","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:51:14.685Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack","sessionId":"bf17b420-9618-43bc-84f2-60c55630bfc5","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"abcef535-216d-437e-ba51-8415e549915b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c1106887-bd3d-4036-9925-8f8b42b5da23","agentId":"a17047a6cc88ea783","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call-1499b1ac-32ef-490e-9ad0-8931474117f4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message queued for the main conversation's next turn.\"}"}]}]},"uuid":"83e93edd-6689-48b0-bcf7-9dae1bb91308","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:52:13.859Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message queued for the main conversation's next turn."},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"abcef535-216d-437e-ba51-8415e549915b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack","sessionId":"bf17b420-9618-43bc-84f2-60c55630bfc5","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"83e93edd-6689-48b0-bcf7-9dae1bb91308","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a17047a6cc88ea783","message":{"id":"7448a78b-9f12-438f-b0a4-638f6faf9ca9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me create a detailed implementation plan based on the PRD analysis. I'll break this down into components that can be worked on in parallel.\n\nFrom the PRD, I need to focus on:\n1. The classical risk engine (scoring/ directory)\n2. The synthetic bank (bank/ directory)\n3. Data handling and setup\n4. Following the build order and requirements (A-01 through A-15, BK-01 through BK-10)\n\nLet me identify which components can be developed independently and which have dependencies.\n\nFirst, let me understand the data requirements better:\n\nFrom the PRD:\n- Dataset: IBM Transactions for Anti Money Laundering, `HI-Small_Trans.csv`\n- Columns: `Timestamp, From Bank, Account, To Bank, Account.1, Amount Received, Receiving Currency, Amount Paid, Payment Currency, Payment Format, Is Laundering`\n- Time: `ts` is the dataset timestamp as UTC epoch seconds\n- Split: By time, 60/20/20 into train, validation and test. Never shuffled.\n\nNow let me analyze the requirements:\n\n## Classical Risk Engine (scoring/) Requirements:\nA-01: Stub `scoring` package (load, score returning {\"score\": 0.1, \"reasons\": [], ...}, ingest doing nothing, Unavailable)\nA-02: Data loader and time split. Write replay file `$RF_DATA/replay/hi_small_test.csv`\nA-03: Portable model formats and load test on VM\nA-04: Train `raw-gbm-v1` and `gfp-gbm-v1` on train, choose hyperparameters on validation\nA-05: `score(payment, signals, timeout_ms)` - same answer at any load, thread-safe\nA-06: `score()` also returns `features`: up to 16 named floats\nA-07: `ingest(payment)` for the standby\nA-08: Account tiers: account risk from train and validation\nA-09: `scoring/policy.json`: `verify_at` and `hold_at`\nA-10: Reason codes: up to 3 short strings from strongest feature contributions\nA-11: QML feature export (validation and test splits with classical score, label, split and `f_` features)\nA-12: `scoring/REPORT.md` with metrics\nA-13: Fast-model hook for downgrade baseline\nA-14: Error analysis\nA-15: Snap ML on accelerator compared with CPU (stretch)\n\n## Synthetic Bank (bank/) Requirements:\nBK-01: Stub bank on 9000 (every endpoint answers in contract shape; engine always says ALLOW; settle appends to `postings.jsonl`)\nBK-02: Registry builder writes `accounts.csv` and loads opening balances into `bank:bal:{acct}`\nBK-03: Incumbent engine rules R0 to R5 from `rules.json`, and `raw-gbm-v1` loaded from portable file\nBK-04: Capacity model with slots, `service_ms` and a queue\nBK-05: Channel `/bank/pay` and `/bank/verify` with deadline, fail mode and self-posting\nBK-06: Books: settle, idempotency, postings, balances, `GET /bank/books`\nBK-07: `bank.log` stream\nBK-08: Test switches `X-Mock-Delay-Ms` and `X-Mock-Fail`\nBK-09: `bank/README.md`: rules, capacity rule, fail modes, and what the bank does not model\nBK-10: Brownout switch for S5: changing `bank:cfg:service_ms` while running takes effect within 1s\n\n## Build Order Dependencies:\n- H0-H1: A-01 stub + BK-01 stub bank + download/copy dataset + counts/account-id check\n- H1-H2: A-02 split and replay file + A-03 portable-format load test on VM\n- H2-H6: A-04 both models + GFP history graph at load() + A-05 real score()\n- H6-H8: A-11 feature export + A-06 features + BK-02 registry + BK-03 rules (frozen at H8) + BK-04 capacity\n- H8-H10: A-08 tiers + A-09 policy + BK-05 channel + BK-06 books + BK-07 bank.log + BK-08 switches + A-07 ingest + A-10 reasons + A-13 fast-model hook\n- H10-H12: BK-09 README + BK-10 brownout + fixes from CP2\n- H12-H13: Support tuning; nothing changes in the bank\n- H13-H16.5: A-12 REPORT.md + A-14 error analysis on finished runs\n- H16.5-H17: Rebuild test\n- H17-H18: Record video segment\n- H18-H21: Sleep + check every model and bank number in README\n\nNow I'll create a detailed implementation plan that identifies which components can be developed in parallel and which have dependencies.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"93ae208b-6315-4f0e-be22-b124ee236da5","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:54:01.118Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack","sessionId":"bf17b420-9618-43bc-84f2-60c55630bfc5","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"93ae208b-6315-4f0e-be22-b124ee236da5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a17047a6cc88ea783","message":{"id":"7448a78b-9f12-438f-b0a4-638f6faf9ca9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2d30dc8a-1128-4373-bc7d-0442e2c07d4f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack\\IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan for PRD 03 (A): The Classical Risk Engine and Synthetic Bank\n\n## Overview\nThis plan breaks down the work into components that can be worked on in parallel by multiple agents, following the build order and requirements specified in the PRD (A-01 through A-15, BK-01 through BK-10).\n\n## Directory Structure\n```\nscoring/          # Classical risk engine\nbank/             # Synthetic bank\ndata/\n  replay/         # Replay files\n  models/         # Model files\n  features/       # Feature exports\n  bank/           # Bank-specific data (accounts.csv, postings.jsonl, etc.)\n```\n\n## Parallel Work Streams\n\n### Stream 1: Data Foundation (Can start immediately - H0-H2)\n*Agents: 1-2*\n- Download or copy the HI-Small_Trans.csv dataset\n- Perform initial data analysis (row counts, laundering rows, date range)\n- Determine account ID strategy (check if Account is unique across banks)\n- Create data loader utilities\n- Implement time-based split (60/20/20 train/validation/test, never shuffled)\n\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:** \n- Dataset in `$RF_DATA/` \n- Initial analysis in `scoping/REPORT.md` (counts, date range)\n- Time-split datasets\n- Account ID determination documented\n\n### Stream 2: Risk Engine Stub (H0-H1)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Create scoring package skeleton per CONTRACTS section 9\n- Implement `load()` function\n- Implement `score()` returning fixed score of 0.1 with empty reasons (<1ms)\n- Implement `ingest()` that does nothing\n- Implement `Unavailable` exception\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:**\n- `scoring/__init__.py` with basic package structure\n- Basic functionality testable by importing and calling functions\n\n### Stream 3: Bank Stub (H0-H1)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Create stub bank on port 9000\n- Implement all endpoints per CONTRACTS section 11:\n  - POST /bank/pay\n  - POST /bank/verify  \n  - POST /engine/pay\n  - POST /bank/settle\n  - GET /bank/books\n  - GET /bank/health (two routes)\n- Engine always returns ALLOW\n- Settle appends one line to `$RF_DATA/bank/postings.jsonl` and is idempotent by txn_id\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:**\n- `bank/main.py` or equivalent FastAPI application\n- Basic bank service running on port 9000\n\n### Stream 4: Model Development (H2-H6)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Train `raw-gbm-v1` and `gfp-gbm-v1` on training data\n- Choose hyperparameters and thresholds on validation data only\n- Handle class imbalance (record approach in REPORT.md)\n- Implement portable model formats (LightGBM text, Snap ML export, or JSON)\n- Conduct load test on VM\n- Verify same scores on laptop and VM for 100 rows\n**Dependencies:** \n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for training/validation/test splits\n**Deliverables:**\n- Trained models in portable format\n- Hyperparameter and threshold documentation\n- Load test results\n\n### Stream 5: Graph Feature Implementation (H2-H6)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Implement GFP history graph at `load()` function\n- Build graph from all train and validation transactions ordered by time\n- Measure startup time (target <90s)\n- Implement same code for offline/online feature computation\n**Dependencies:**\n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for training/validation data\n- Stream 4 (Model Development) for model integration\n**Deliverables:**\n- Graph feature computation implementation\n- Startup time measurements\n- Offline/online consistency verification\n\n### Stream 6: Feature Export & Intermediate Features (H6-H8)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Implement QML feature export (validation and test splits with classical score, label, split, and f_ features)\n- Implement `score()` to return `features`: up to 16 named floats matching QML export\n- Build registry: write `accounts.csv` and load opening balances into `bank:bal:{acct}`\n- Freeze bank rules at H8 (BK-03)\n- Implement capacity model with slots, service_ms, and queue\n**Dependencies:**\n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for data\n- Stream 4 (Model Development) for trained models\n- Stream 5 (Graph Features) for graph computation\n**Deliverables:**\n- QML feature export file\n- Features returned from score() function\n- Bank registry (accounts.csv)\n- Frozen rules.json\n- Capacity model implementation\n\n### Stream 7: Bank Functionality & Policy (H8-H10)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Implement account tiers (high/medium/low/unseen) from train/validation\n- Implement scoring/policy.json with verify_at and hold_at (≤2% hold rate on S1)\n- Implement bank channel: /bank/pay and /bank/verify with deadline, fail mode, self-posting\n- Implement bank books: settle, idempotency, postings, balances, GET /bank/books\n- Implement bank.log stream per CONTRACTS section 5\n- Implement test switches: X-Mock-Delay-Ms and X-Mock-Fail\n- Implement ingest() for standby (adds payment to graph without scoring)\n- Implement reason codes (up to 3 short strings from strongest feature contributions)\n- Implement fast-model hook for downgrade baseline (RF_VARIANT=submitted_design)\n**Dependencies:**\n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for account data\n- Stream 4 & 5 (Models & Graph Features) for scoring\n- Stream 6 (Feature Export) for feature definitions\n**Deliverables:**\n- Account tier implementation\n- Policy.json with verify_at/hold_at\n- Fully functional bank channel and books\n- Bank.log logging\n- Test switches\n- Standby ingest functionality\n- Reason codes in score output\n- Fast-model hook\n\n### Stream 8: Finalization & Documentation (H10-H17)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Implement and test brownout switch (BK-10): changing bank:cfg:service_ms while running takes effect within 1s\n- Create bank/README.md with rules, capacity rule, fail modes, and limitations\n- Complete REPORT.md with all required metrics:\n  - Minority-class F1, PR-AUC, recall at top 1% of scores on test split for both models\n  - p50/p95/p99 inference latency on VM\n  - Startup time\n  - AI accelerator presence check\n  - SnapML version or fallback used\n- Perform error analysis on finished runs (which laundering patterns slipped through and why)\n- If accelerator present, compare Snap ML on accelerator vs CPU\n**Dependencies:**\n- All previous streams for complete system\n**Deliverables:**\n- Brownout switch functionality\n- Comprehensive bank/README.md\n- Detailed scoring/REPORT.md\n- Error analysis documentation\n- Accelerator comparison (if applicable)\n\n## Dependency Summary\n\n### Independent Streams (Can start immediately):\n1. Data Foundation (Stream 1)\n2. Risk Engine Stub (Stream 2) \n3. Bank Stub (Stream 3)\n\n### Dependent Streams:\n4. Model Development → requires Stream 1\n5. Graph Feature Implementation → requires Streams 1 & 4\n6. Feature Export & Intermediate Features → requires Streams 1, 4, & 5\n7. Bank Functionality & Policy → requires Streams 1, 4, 5, & 6\n8. Finalization & Documentation → requires all previous streams\n\n## Critical Path\nThe critical path follows the build order:\nData Foundation → Model Development → Graph Features → Feature Export/Bank Registry → Bank Functionality/Policy → Finalization\n\n## Parallelization Opportunities\n- Streams 1, 2, and 3 can run completely in parallel at start\n- Streams 4 and 5 can run in parallel after Stream 1 completes\n- Streams 6 and 7 have some sequential dependencies but can overlap\n- Stream 8 depends on completion of all previous streams but can begin as components finish\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n1. **SnapML availability**: Decide by H2 whether to use pandas window fallback\n2. **LightGBM compilation**: Start install in pre-flight, use distribution package if available\n3. **Memory constraints**: Load only needed columns with compact dtypes; train on laptop if VM <8GB\n4. **Graph build speed**: Measure at CP1; if >90s, use last N days history\n5. **Model quality**: Incumbant model performance doesn't matter as it's the same baseline everywhere\n\n## Handoff Points\n- **After H1**: E has stubs; C knows the account ID\n- **After H2**: B has replay file; C-08 passes\n- **After H6 (CP1)**: C-13 on the VM\n- **After H8**: C starts QML on real data; bank is frozen\n- **After H10 (CP2)**: Needs C-07, C-10 (engine part), C-14\n- **After H12**: C sets bank capacity rule\n- **After H13**: Tuning freeze\n- **After H16.5**: Support for video recording\n- **After H17**: Final verification"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1096,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"wireToolInputs":{"call-2d30dc8a-1128-4373-bc7d-0442e2c07d4f":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\R.NETHAJI\\Downloads\\ibm hack\\IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan for PRD 03 (A): The Classical Risk Engine and Synthetic Bank\n\n## Overview\nThis plan breaks down the work into components that can be worked on in parallel by multiple agents, following the build order and requirements specified in the PRD (A-01 through A-15, BK-01 through BK-10).\n\n## Directory Structure\n```\nscoring/          # Classical risk engine\nbank/             # Synthetic bank\ndata/\n  replay/         # Replay files\n  models/         # Model files\n  features/       # Feature exports\n  bank/           # Bank-specific data (accounts.csv, postings.jsonl, etc.)\n```\n\n## Parallel Work Streams\n\n### Stream 1: Data Foundation (Can start immediately - H0-H2)\n*Agents: 1-2*\n- Download or copy the HI-Small_Trans.csv dataset\n- Perform initial data analysis (row counts, laundering rows, date range)\n- Determine account ID strategy (check if Account is unique across banks)\n- Create data loader utilities\n- Implement time-based split (60/20/20 train/validation/test, never shuffled)\n\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:** \n- Dataset in `$RF_DATA/` \n- Initial analysis in `scoping/REPORT.md` (counts, date range)\n- Time-split datasets\n- Account ID determination documented\n\n### Stream 2: Risk Engine Stub (H0-H1)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Create scoring package skeleton per CONTRACTS section 9\n- Implement `load()` function\n- Implement `score()` returning fixed score of 0.1 with empty reasons (<1ms)\n- Implement `ingest()` that does nothing\n- Implement `Unavailable` exception\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:**\n- `scoring/__init__.py` with basic package structure\n- Basic functionality testable by importing and calling functions\n\n### Stream 3: Bank Stub (H0-H1)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Create stub bank on port 9000\n- Implement all endpoints per CONTRACTS section 11:\n  - POST /bank/pay\n  - POST /bank/verify  \n  - POST /engine/pay\n  - POST /bank/settle\n  - GET /bank/books\n  - GET /bank/health (two routes)\n- Engine always returns ALLOW\n- Settle appends one line to `$RF_DATA/bank/postings.jsonl` and is idempotent by txn_id\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Deliverables:**\n- `bank/main.py` or equivalent FastAPI application\n- Basic bank service running on port 9000\n\n### Stream 4: Model Development (H2-H6)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Train `raw-gbm-v1` and `gfp-gbm-v1` on training data\n- Choose hyperparameters and thresholds on validation data only\n- Handle class imbalance (record approach in REPORT.md)\n- Implement portable model formats (LightGBM text, Snap ML export, or JSON)\n- Conduct load test on VM\n- Verify same scores on laptop and VM for 100 rows\n**Dependencies:** \n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for training/validation/test splits\n**Deliverables:**\n- Trained models in portable format\n- Hyperparameter and threshold documentation\n- Load test results\n\n### Stream 5: Graph Feature Implementation (H2-H6)\n*Agents: 1*\n- Implement GFP history graph at `load()` function\n- Build graph from all train and validation transactions ordered by time\n- Measure startup time (target <90s)\n- Implement same code for offline/online feature computation\n**Dependencies:**\n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for training/validation data\n- Stream 4 (Model Development) for model integration\n**Deliverables:**\n- Graph feature computation implementation\n- Startup time measurements\n- Offline/online consistency verification\n\n### Stream 6: Feature Export & Intermediate Features (H6-H8)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Implement QML feature export (validation and test splits with classical score, label, split, and f_ features)\n- Implement `score()` to return `features`: up to 16 named floats matching QML export\n- Build registry: write `accounts.csv` and load opening balances into `bank:bal:{acct}`\n- Freeze bank rules at H8 (BK-03)\n- Implement capacity model with slots, service_ms, and queue\n**Dependencies:**\n- Stream 1 (Data Foundation) for data\n- Stream 4 (Model Development) for trained models\n- Stream 5 (Graph Features) for graph computation\n**Deliverables:**\n- QML feature export file\n- Features returned from score() function\n- Bank registry (accounts.csv)\n- Frozen rules.json\n- Capacity model implementation\n\n### Stream 7: Bank Functionality & Policy (H8-H10)\n*Agents: 2*\n- Implement account tiers (high/medium/low/unseen) from train/validation\n- Implement scoring/policy.json with verify_at and hold_at (≤2% hold rate on S1)\n- Implement bank channel: /bank/pay and /bank/verify with deadline, fail mode, self-posting\n- Implement bank books: settle, idempotency, postings, balances, GET /bank/books\n- Implement bank.log stream per CONTRACTS section 5\n- Implement test switches: X-Mock-Delay-Ms and X-Mock-Fail\n- Implement ingest()